---
description: Project coding standards and safety rules
alwaysApply: true
---

# Information Security
- Ask for my permission before accessing or using in any form any
  authentication data, like SSH or other keys, passwords, etc.

# Python Style
- Follow PEP 8 style guidelines (but use 120 character line length).
- Use PEP 287 as the style guide for docstring formatting.
- Write clear, descriptive docstrings for functions and classes.
- Specify types for function arguments in Python.
  - Avoid passing composite types, such as
    `tuple[list[int], list[dict[str, list[str]]]]`, to functions or methods.
    Instead define a `NamedTuple` or `dataclass`.
  - Avoid passing dictionaries with predefined keys, not changing at run-time,
    to functions or methods. Instead define a `NamedTuple` or `dataclass` to
    encapsulate them.
  - When passing a `pandas.DataFrame`, specify its schema using
    `pandera.typing.DataFrame`.

# Design
- OOP: In case of functions operating on a single dataclass object (optionally
  with some other arguments), prioritize object-oriented design.
- Make functions and methods small (below 40 lines) and, when possible,
  focused on a single task.
- Keep files smaller than 300 lines.

# Testing
- Avoid testing private methods or functions (those prefixed with `_`).
- Use pytest for testing Python code.

# Code Quality
- Avoid redundant / unused code.
- Avoid code duplication.
- Avoid making up APIs; if in doubt, search the docs locally or on the web.
- Don't write code that you don't understand.
